  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Terri Bolton is a {dab hand} when it comes to {DIY} (do-it-yourself). {Skilled} at doing odd jobs around the house, such as {piecing} together {furniture} , {fixing pipes} and {wires} , {she} never pays {someone else} to do a job she can do {herself} .",
      "cn": "说到DIY（ 自己动手做 ），泰莉·博尔顿可是个 能手 。 她擅长 做家里的各种零活，比如 组装家具 ， 修理管道 和 电线 ， 她自己 能做的事从不花钱雇 别人 做。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "She credits these skills to her late {grandfather} and {builder} Derek Lloyd.From the age of {six} , Terri, now 26, accompanied Derek to work during her school {holidays} .A day's work was rewarded with £5 in {pocket money} .She says:\"I'm sure I wasn't much of a help to start with, painting the rooms and putting down the {flooring throughout} the {house} .It took weeks and it was {backbreaking} work, but I know he was proud of my skills.\"",
      "cn": "她把这些技能归功于自己已故的 祖父 —— 建筑工人 德里克·劳埃德。如今26岁的泰莉从 六 岁起就在学校 放假 期间陪着德里克去干活，干一天活会被奖励5英镑的 零花钱 。她说：\"一开始我肯定没帮上多大忙，只是粉刷房间和为 整 栋 房子 铺 地板 。这花了几个星期，而且是 累人的 差事，但我知道他为我的技能感到骄傲。\""
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "{Ms.} Bolton, who now {rents} a house with friends in Wandsworth, {South West London} , says DIY also saves her from losing any {deposit} when a tenancy ( (租期) ) comes to an end.She adds:\"I've moved house many times and I always like to {personalize} my {flat} and put up {pictures} , so it's been {useful} to know how to cover up {holes} and {repaint} a room to avoid any {charges} when I've moved out.\"With a pair of {gloves} and sturdy {boots} , she tackled everything from repairing the {roof} to {installing} new {plugs} and {nails} , measuring in {centimeters} to ensure safety.",
      "cn": "博尔顿 女士 现在和朋友们在 伦敦西南部 的旺兹沃思 租 了一套房子，她说，DIY还能让她在租约到期时避免损失 押金 。她补充说：\"我搬过很多次家，我总是喜欢让 公寓 更 具个人风格 ，还会挂上一些 画 。所以，知道如何遮盖墙上的 洞 和 重新粉刷 房间都是非常 有用的 ，可以在我搬走时避免被扣 费 。\"她戴着一副 手套 ，穿着结实的 靴子 ，从修补 屋顶 到 安装 新的 插座 和 钉子 ，什么活儿都干，测量时精确到 厘米 ，以确保安全。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "With {millions} of people likely to take on DIY projects over the {coming} weeks, new research shows that more than {half} of people are planning to make the most of the long, warm {summer} days to get jobs done.The average {spend per} project will be around £823. {Two thirds} of people aim to improve their comfort while at home.Two {fifths} wish to increase the value of their house.Though DIY has traditionally been seen as a {male hobby} , the research shows it is women who are now leading the charge.People craft everything from {cute scarf hangers} to {lanterns} for the garden.",
      "cn": "接下来的 几周，可能会有数 百万 人参与DIY项目。一项新的调查显示，超过 一半 的人计划充分利用漫长而温暖的 夏 日完成这些工作。 每个 项目的平均 花费 约为823英镑。 三分之二 的人打算提升居家舒适度。 五分之 二的人希望提高房屋价值。虽然DIY在传统上一直被视为一项 男性的爱好 ，但该调查显示，现在是女性在引领这一潮流。人们亲手制作各种物品，从 可爱的围巾挂架 到花园里的 灯笼 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Alex Gosling, the boss of online estate agency HouseSimple, warns people to recognize their DIY limitations.You might find a {leak} in the bathroom that almost ruins all your {clay} tiles ( (瓷砖) ).Or you might try to hang a {vase} , only to realize you need better support beams ( (梁) ).\"We're probably all capable of painting walls, but it's a big step to building an {extension} or taking load-bearing walls down.\"",
      "cn": "在线房地产中介机构HouseSimple的老板亚历克斯·高斯林提醒人们，要认清自己在DIY方面的能力局限。你可能会发现浴室有一处 漏水的地方 ，它差点毁了你所有的 陶土 瓷砖。或者，你可能试图挂一个 花瓶 ，却发现你需要更坚固的支撑梁。\"粉刷墙壁或许人人都会，但要进行房屋 扩建 或拆除承重墙，那就是一个巨大的飞跃了。\" 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    }
  ],
